{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790966786,"nonce":"nOn8S6t5mzApxuon/I1PcWISilI=","title":"css-only compositor fast path overwrote cached_dynamic_batch with an empty walked batch","message":"In the compositor's css-only fast path, `cached_dynamic_batch` used to be unconditionally overwritten with whatever `collect_dynamic_region_primitives` returned. That function intentionally filters out `DynamicKind::CssAnimated` and `DynamicKind::Canvas` (both paint through their own paths). When the only DynamicRegions present are those two kinds, the filtered ordered set is empty and the function returns `PrimitiveBatch::new()`. Writing that empty batch into `cached_dynamic_batch` wipes the prior slow-walker-captured overlay-subtree primitives.\n\n**Symptom**: open `cn::context_menu` and hover a submenu-trigger row. The submenu opens with its `cn-context-menu-enter` CSS keyframe playing. The parent menu's panel bg + border + item `:hover` bg vanish from the surface for the duration of the submenu's enter (~200ms). Text glyphs and SVG shortcuts in the parent menu keep painting because they ride `cached_motion_subtree_text_prims` / `cached_motion_subtree_svgs`, dispatched independently. When the submenu settles, the slow walker runs again and the parent's bg/border return.\n\n**Why text/SVG survive while SDF disappears**: the css-only fast path only touches `cached_dynamic_batch`. Text + SVG live in their own caches, so they paint regardless of what happens to the SDF batch.\n\n**Mechanism**:\n1. OverlayStack push fires a Structural rebuild. Slow walker emits parent menu's bg/border/item-hover-bg into `dynamic_batch` via the `is_overlay_root → push_motion_subtree` gate. Captured into `cached_dynamic_batch`. Submenu registers a `DynamicKind::CssAnimated` region and bakes a `LayerTexture`.\n2. Subsequent frames: `css_only_active = true` (submenu's animation playing). Fast path runs `collect_dynamic_region_primitives`. With only `CssAnimated` (submenu) + `Canvas` (node-editor canvas) in `dynamic_regions`, the filter leaves nothing → empty batch.\n3. Empty batch overwrites `cached_dynamic_batch`. `dispatch_dynamic_batch_overlay` short-circuits on `primitives.is_empty()`. Parent menu's SDF primitives are not painted.\n4. Submenu settles → fast path drops out → slow walker emits parent again → bg/border return.\n\n**Fix**: gate the assignment on `walked.primitives.is_empty()`. Two sites in `crates/blinc_app/src/context.rs`: the `css_patch_eligible` fast path (~7759) and the `use_fast` path (~8123). When the re-walk genuinely produces no primitives, preserve the prior slow-walker batch.\n\n**Generalizes to**: any stacked overlay where one entry's CSS animation is mid-flight while a sibling's is settled — popover-inside-popover, dropdown-inside-popover, toast appearing while a popover's enter is playing.\n\n**How to apply**: when an overlay routes through `is_overlay_root` (so its primitives go into `dynamic_batch`) and a sibling overlay's CSS animation registers a `CssAnimated` DynamicRegion, the cached dyn-batch from the previous slow walk MUST survive the css-only fast path. The fast path's role is to refresh `MotionSubtree` (non-promoted) regions, not to replace the whole batch.\n\n**Don't**: try to \"fix\" by adding `CssAnimated` or `Canvas` back into `collect_dynamic_region_primitives` — they're filtered for a reason (composite-promoted CSS animations paint via `composite_css_layers_overlay`, canvases have their own DPI-correct path).\n\n**Don't**: rely on CSS-side workarounds like `.cn-context-menu:has(...) { background: var(--surface-elevated); }` to compensate. The parent's bg is being wiped at the compositor cache level, not at the render-props level.\n\nRelated: [[gotcha-css-anim-eager-drain]] (separate but related — eager animation drain caused the visually-similar opacity flicker; this gotcha is about the SDF dispatch path).","files":null}]}